sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User Browser
    participant C as Client Application
    participant OP as OpenID Provider
    participant API as Application Backend
    C->>C: Create state, nonce, code verifier and code challenge
    C->>U: Redirect to provider with state, nonce and challenge
    U->>OP: Authenticate user
    OP-->>U: Redirect to registered callback with code and state
    U->>C: Callback with code and state
    C->>C: Verify state matches the initiating request
    C->>OP: Redeem code with code verifier
    OP-->>C: Tokens
    C->>C: Validate ID token signature, issuer, audience, expiry and nonce
    C->>API: Establish local session or complete documented client flow
    Note over C,OP: Use a maintained OIDC client; this diagram is conceptual
